**suggestion:** Consider whether the `branch` field should be reflected in the GitHub URL.

`DocsGitConfig` includes a `branch`, but `createBaseLayoutOptions` ignores it and always links to the repo root. Either include `/tree/${gitConfig.branch}` (or similar) when appropriate, or remove `branch` from `DocsGitConfig` if it’s not needed to avoid confusion.

Suggested implementation:

```typescript
export function createBaseLayoutOptions(
  title: string,
  gitConfig: DocsGitConfig,
  docsUrl = "/docs",
): DocsBaseLayoutProps {
  const baseGithubUrl = `https://github.com/${gitConfig.user}/${gitConfig.repo}`;
  const githubUrl = gitConfig.branch
    ? `${baseGithubUrl}/tree/${gitConfig.branch}`
    : baseGithubUrl;

  return {
    nav: {
      title,
      url: docsUrl,
    },
    githubUrl,
  };
}

```

1. Ensure the `DocsGitConfig` type includes an optional `branch?: string;` field (or required, depending on your design).
2. If there are other helpers that construct GitHub URLs from `DocsGitConfig`, consider updating them to respect `branch` in a consistent way.

